    "note": "Thresholds are a domain judgment call pending review against FACSI's actual filter sets (K-3, instruments/objectives/lines/detectors, not yet authored). Emission proximity is the primary (error-severity) check: typical bandpass emission filters are 20-40 nm wide and many dye/FP emission curves have a 40-60 nm FWHM, so peaks this close will substantially co-register in each other's detection window regardless of exact filter choice. Excitation proximity is secondary (warning-severity): standard laser lines are spaced 40-100+ nm apart specifically so one line excites one dye class. Each fluorophore now also carries its own emissionFwhmNm (claude-drafted, class-based: e.g. BODIPY dyes are famously narrow, PI/DRAQ5/7AAD/EthD-1/DAPI/Hoechst famously broad/red-tailed once DNA-bound) so the explanatory plot's curve widths differ by fluorophore instead of sharing one shape; schematicEmissionFwhmNm remains the fallback for any fluorophore that somehow lacks one. Neither is a measured spectrum -- still not a quantitative spillover integral."
